From 4a771711841f9bd6ec603fd6ca8ecee97f888d60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valdijanio Vieira <48389119+valdijanio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:57:36 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ospfd: don't assert on a missing router-LSA in the TI-LFA
 reverse SPF

With "fast-reroute ti-lfa", ospf_ti_lfa_generate_q_spaces() builds each
Q space as a reverse SPF tree (area->spf_reversed). For a point-to-point
link V->W, ospf_spf_next() reads the reverse distance from W's
router-LSA in get_reverse_distance() before it checks that W's LSA is in
the LSDB at all (RFC 2328 16.1 (2b), the "w_lsa == NULL" check a few
lines below). When V's router-LSA already advertises a link to a router
whose own router-LSA is not in the LSDB (it has not arrived yet while
adjacencies come up, or it was flushed), the lookup returns NULL and
ospfd aborts:

  ospf_spf.c:1269: get_reverse_distance(): assertion (w_lsa && w_lsa->data) failed

The forward SPF just skips W in that case. Do the same in the reverse
SPF: only read the reverse distance when the LSA was found, and let the
existing check skip W.

Signed-off-by: Valdijanio Vieira <48389119+valdijanio@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 ospfd/ospf_spf.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ospfd/ospf_spf.c b/ospfd/ospf_spf.c
index eee48fe392..c3d2e62d10 100644
--- a/ospfd/ospf_spf.c
+++ b/ospfd/ospf_spf.c
@@ -1404,9 +1404,14 @@ static void ospf_spf_next(struct vertex *v, struct ospf_area *area,
 			/*
 			 * For TI-LFA we might need the reverse SPF.
 			 * Currently only works with P2P!
+			 *
+			 * W's router-LSA may not be in the LSDB (not received
+			 * yet, or already flushed) while V still advertises
+			 * the link: then there is no reverse distance to read,
+			 * and the check below skips W, as the forward SPF does.
 			 */
 			if (type == LSA_LINK_TYPE_POINTOPOINT
-			    && area->spf_reversed)
+			    && area->spf_reversed && w_lsa)
 				link_distance =
 					get_reverse_distance(v, l, w_lsa);
 			else
